    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296-a4">

                <pb facs="0529" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg469"/>

                <head>Letter from the ex-Governor of Puebla.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Diario Oficial, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-19">May 19,
                        1868</date>.—Translation.]</dateline></opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tetela de Ocampo,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 16, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Editor of the Diario Oficial, Mexico:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> In number 135 of the paper which you
                    edit, corresponding to the 14th of the present month, I have seen a document
                    bearing the names of various chiefs.</p>
                <p>As among these names I find my own, and as I have not signed the said document, I
                    beg of you that you will be pleased to make this known to the public by
                    inserting the present letter in your paper, which favor will be duly recognized
                    by your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. N. MENDEZ.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
